  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. Each lottery has two outcomes, so the threshold for an outcome to be considered 'probable' is 1 divided by 2, i.e., 50%. In Lottery A, the outcome of -6000 Euros has a probability of 0.1% (well below 50%), and 0 Euros has 99.9% (above 50%). Thus, only the 0 Euro outcome is 'probable' in A. In Lottery B, -3000 Euros has 0.2% (below 50%), and 0 Euros has 99.8% (above 50%), so again, only the 0 Euro outcome is 'probable'. The average of the probable outcomes is 0 for both lotteries. Therefore, according to the decision reason, the individual should be indifferent between A and B.",
